From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Shape Healing - guard the null Context() in
 ShapeFix_Face::FixPeriodicDegenerated

ShapeFix_Face::Perform crashes (uncatchable SIGSEGV) fixing a face whose sole
boundary wire is a single closed edge that belts the full 2*PI period of a
Geom_ConicalSurface (a rivet/boss-rim seam mesh-fit as one periodic curve is a
common source of exactly this shape), positioned so the cone's apex sits
outside the wire's V range -- the case FixPeriodicDegenerated exists to patch
in a degenerate apex edge for.

Root cause: FixPeriodicDegenerated builds the apex edge/wire, assembles a new
face from the original wire plus the apex wire, and finalizes:

    myResult = aNewFace;
    Context()->Replace(myFace, myResult);

Every OTHER Context()->Replace call site in this same file (eleven of them)
guards against a null Context() first -- e.g. this file's own ComposeShell
path a few hundred lines up:

    if (Context().IsNull())
    {
      SetContext(new ShapeBuild_ReShape);
    }
    ...
    Context()->Replace(myFace, myResult);

or the plain guard used everywhere else:

    if (!Context().IsNull())
    {
      Context()->Replace(...);
    }

FixPeriodicDegenerated's own function header even checks Context().IsNull()
at its TOP before calling Context()->Apply() -- but the check is missing at
the BOTTOM, where Context()->Replace() is called unconditionally. Context()
returns the ShapeFix_Root::myContext handle, which the base constructor
leaves null; it is only ever set by an explicit SetContext() call, which is
optional and NOT made by a bare "ShapeFix_Face fixer(face); fixer.Perform();"
-- the ordinary, most common way to use this class (and the way this file's
own class documentation examples use it). So any caller that fixes a lone
periodic-conical wire without first calling SetContext() null-derefs.

The fix restores the same guard used at every other call site in the file:
only replace in the context if there is a context to replace in. When there
is none, myFace already local-only equals its own fixed state via myResult,
matching the intent (and behavior) of every guarded sibling call site.

Validation (fast path, no full rebuild -- see Scripts/patches/README.md's
#0001 entry for the override-link technique): a synthetic single closed edge
(GeomAPI_Interpolate, closed=true, 10 real mesh-derived points from a rivet
rim) trimmed to a Geom_ConicalSurface via BRepBuilderAPI_MakeFace(surf, wire,
true), then healed with a bare "ShapeFix_Face fixer(face); fixer.Perform();"
SIGSEGVs 100% of the time on stock V8_0_0_p1 (backtrace_symbols_fd, since
lldb/core-dumps were unavailable in the diagnosing environment, pinpoints the
crash to ShapeFix_Face::FixPeriodicDegenerated's Context()->Replace call, one
statement past the last successful trace line before the fix); after this
patch the same input returns IsDone()==true and BRepCheck_Analyzer(fixed)
.IsValid()==true. Statement-level tracing (-O0 single-TU override-link)
confirms every prior line in the function returns/completes normally and the
crash is specifically the unguarded Context()->Replace call.

Reported downstream and isolated at SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#317.
---
 src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_Face.cxx | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_Face.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_Face.cxx
index 48ae1347..8db05eee 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_Face.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_Face.cxx
@@ -3268,7 +3268,11 @@ bool ShapeFix_Face::FixPeriodicDegenerated()

   // Adjust the resulting state of the healing tool
   myResult = aNewFace;
-  Context()->Replace(myFace, myResult);
+  // #317: guard null Context(), as every other Replace() call site in this file does
+  if (!Context().IsNull())
+  {
+    Context()->Replace(myFace, myResult);
+  }

   return true;
 }
